      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Most patients who need dental implantation suffer from somatic diseases. Therefore, an anesthesiologist's participation is highly desirable, since he supports the stability of vital functions. The authors used mixed anesthesia involving traditional field-block and general anesthesia. By choosing doses of anesthetics, the authors achieved ataraxia which preserved the minimum contact with a patient and a complete analgesia, which gave rise to psychoemotional stability."},
